president Trump's daughter and  son-in-law face criticism over their use  of private emails and text messages for  government business in a letter to the  White House House Oversight Committee  Chairman Elijah come and said the  communications of Ivanka Trump and Jared  Kushner raise security and  record-keeping concerns  he threatened to use quote alternative  means if the White House does not  provide more information Paula Reid is  at the White House with more on this  story Paula good morning good morning  president Trump spent much of the 2016  campaign criticizing Hillary Clinton for  her use of personal email  he even accused her of mishandling  classified information now those same  allegations are being made against his  own family an attorney for the  president's son-in-law Jared Kushner  admits Kushner used the encrypted  messaging program whatsapp in his  official duties including communications  with people outside the US the attorney  also confirms Ivanka Trump received  official email on her personal account  until September 2017 now senior White  House officials are prohibited from  using personal accounts for work unless  they copy an official account or forward  the message now Kushner's lawyer insists  that screenshots of his messages were  forwarded for archiving but he cannot  say whether Kushner ever sent classified  information via the app mishandling  classified information can result in  criminal charges the White House Counsel  tells CBS News it will review  congressman Cummings requests for  additional information now in a separate  request the White House is rejecting  demands from Democratic investigators  for details of the president's  conversations with Vladimir Putin the  White House insists the president's  conversations with foreign leaders are  confidential Gail thank you Paul
 

